{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310826,"nonce":"Ga/dMfMgYx7H6KEta3Kpdeagris=","title":"The corpus denominator went 407 -\u003e 1030 on 2026-08-25. It was never 407: the selector hid 714 files, which hid a real resolution bug. Do ...","message":"**The conformance denominator changed on 2026-08-25: 407 -\u003e 1030 scored.**\nA score from before that date is NOT comparable with one after. The old number\nwas not a subset chosen on purpose -- it was a bug.\n\n\n`haxe-conformance/run.sh` selected tests with `grep \"extends unit.Test\"`. Of the\n1165 issue files, only 451 spell it that way; the other **714 write\n`extends Test`** and were dropped BEFORE compilation -- missing from the\nnumerator and the denominator, and absent from the report entirely. Every one of\nthe 1165 is a real test; none are helpers.\n\n\nThe 714 were exactly the files rayzor could not compile: **a bare type name did\nnot resolve to a type in an ENCLOSING package**. `unit.issues.IssueNNNN` naming\n`unit.Test` as plain `Test` got a placeholder supertype, so every inherited\n`eq`/`t` reported \"Cannot find name\". Widening the selector without fixing\nresolution would have shown 714 fresh failures; fixing resolution without\nwidening would have shown nothing at all.\n\nFixed in `compilation.rs::enclosing_package_candidates` (called where\n`all_imports` is assembled): for a bare supertype, offer\n`\u003cpackage minus k segments\u003e.\u003cName\u003e`, nearest first. They go through\n`load_imports_efficiently`, so they resolve against EVERY class path -- a\nsibling from a separate library is found by NAMESPACE, not folder adjacency\n(the owner called this out explicitly). Unmatched candidates cost a failed\npath lookup and nothing else.\n\n\n| | old selector | full corpus |\n|---|---|---|\n| scored | 407 | 1030 |\n| PASS | 135 | 321 |\n\nThe 451 already counted kept their status EXACTLY (0 gained, 0 lost).\nOf the 714 newly visible: 186 PASS, 226 COMPILE_FAIL, 105 CRASH,\n102 WRONG_ANSWER, 91 SKIP, 4 TIMEOUT.\n\n\nAn entry in a nested package fails to compile when the class path is a\nSUBDIRECTORY rather than `\".\"` -- \"No MIR modules generated\". Reproduces with an\nexplicit `import` too, so it is not name resolution. This blocks verifying\ncross-CLASS-PATH sibling resolution end to end; same-root is verified.\n\nRelated: [[bugs-xmodule-resolution-disease-cluster]].\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_conformance_denominator_and_sibling_types` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}